+# APEX Connect — signed login-only PRE/POST cutover execution boundary
+
+**Date:** 14 October 2026. **Engineering status:** Source complete; production NO-GO.
+**Scope:** APEX Connect teacher login only. No academic mark publication, no
+Principal impersonation, and no credential extraction or real data writes.
+
+## Permanent architecture
+
+The existing login-only release verifier historically required all THREE
+real postflight receipts before traffic promotion:
+1. Existing authorized teacher signed live browser acceptance.
+2. Independent signed live cross-school and unauthorized subject HTTP denial.
+3. Actual live traffic rollback executed under SaaS Core release ownership.
+
+The third item is inherently POST-cutover evidence and must not be forged
+or called complete before traffic has ever been switched. It remains a
+required FINAL CERTIFICATION, never a permission to bypass safe preflight.
+
+A new strictly read-only PRE-CUTOVER verifier has been implemented at:
+scripts/connect/verify-signed-precutover-contract-20261014.cjs
+
+It validates, in one coordinated review:
+- Source SHA of reviewed auth proxy and actual compiled candidate BUILD_ID.
+- Exact live Blue Nginx SHA, preserved old dashboard intercept baseline.
+- Green Nginx file private loopback upstream, removal of both unconditional
+  dashboard-to-admin locations, no old Next config redirect.
+- Actual root-private full database backup exact SHA.
+- Independently recorded SaaS Core **login-only** safety gate, whose status
+  must be READY_FOR_LOGIN_ONLY_CORE, signed tenant runtime security must be
+  certified, and official academic results must remain unpublished.
+- A genuine owner-pinned root-owned Ed25519 public key under
+  /etc/assps/release-evidence-ed25519.pub (no local fake key installed).
+- Core-release-owner signed, non-stale attestation over EXACT release ID,
+  source SHA, Next build ID, origin, Blue+Green Nginx hashes, backup digest
+  and Core status artifact digest. It must expressly verify signed tenant
+  and peer-school denial, correct compiled artifacts, recovery rehearsal,
+  unchanged marks and no academic result publication.
+
+The verifier NEVER switches traffic, signs a human receipt, obtains passwords,
+modifies production records or certifies final public release. Its positive
+result is only READY_FOR_SAAS_CORE_CONTROLLED_SWITCH, not RELEASE_CERTIFIED.
+
+The original existing post-release signed verifier remains separately required
+for real authenticated teacher browser session, peer-school/subject denials,
+compiled deployed build and **actual completed live traffic rollback**.
+A source or synthetic test pass is not post-release actor certification.
+
+## Actual source and live evidence
+
+Previous combined real TLS Chromium acceptance on restored school PostgreSQL,
+with synthetic teacher and isolated browser HTTPS ingress: 15/15 PASS. That
+is genuine browser code testing, not genuine existing Muhammad Imran login.
+
+New negative tests:
+- PRE-cutover signed source/actor/rollback artifact: 15/15 PASS.
+- Older signed-release negative suite: 10/10 PASS.
+- Nginx Blue/Green routing negatives: 9/9 PASS.
+- Existing teacher postlogin redirect: 19/19 PASS.
+- Auth path exclusions: 12/12 PASS.
+- Canonical role / fake Host boundaries: 9/9 PASS.
+
+A NEW actual read-only source/live preflight was executed with the currently
+reviewed compiled Next candidate ONDwxEIZlx5onDIKY7wYf and a PRIVATE
+staged corrected copy of the ACTUAL production Nginx virtual host. Current
+Nginx and PostgreSQL production files were NOT modified or reloaded.
+
+**Actual PRE result: HOLD.** Source SHA, compiled candidate BUILD_ID, exact
+Blue Nginx, isolated Green candidate and full backup digest all PASS.
+Core independently signed live runtime acceptance, genuinely owner-pinned
+public key and genuine signed Core-owner receipt remain MISSING/FAIL.
+
+The existing public Next BUILD_ID remains XI7EvxpUMkKOxK5ByM2BH; live
+/dashboard still 307 to /admin. Corrected app has not reached public users.
+
+## Core owner release sequence with no fabricated institutional decisions
+
+A. Prepare and verify current Core signed tenant runtime, distinct global
+worker and independent real peer-school HTTP denial; preserve Blue, full
+current backup and off-host recovery under established owner custody.
+Core must issue an independently genuine status artifact and trusted root.
+
+B. With these actual artifacts, run the new PRE verifier against reviewed
+compiled Next and private Green Nginx. PASS is a necessary, not sufficient,
+condition for an authorized atomic Next + Nginx traffic switch.
+
+C. After a successful controlled cutover, obtain actual teacher temporary
+password rotation / new login / signed session behavior, independent
+cross-tenant denial, and Core-owned real traffic rollback evidence, then
+run the original POST verifier. Revert to Blue on failures and recheck
+ExamID9 protected marks. Mark LIVE release certified only with genuine
+postflight evidence, not synthetic actor/signature proofs.
+
+Official subject maximum mark approvals and published results are entirely
+separate release tracks, never auto-approved to unblock login.
+
+**No production service, staff credential, API token, RLS policy, teacher
+assignment, marks or school records changed in this source mission.**
